{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"Aligned storage recovers roughly 20% on each irregular workload. The next larger bottleneck is redundant input traffic: each 128×128 block reloads both operands. I’m prototyping a persistent head/tile kernel that holds one query or key tile in registers while sweeping the other output dimension, which can remove nearly half of those input reads on long sequences."}}
