{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"The persistent sweep is correct in structure but does not beat the tiled kernel—the saved reads are already largely served by cache, while the longer-lived workgroups lose scheduling efficiency. I’m keeping the simpler tiled path, applying only the measured aligned-row improvement and a 64×64 choice for the short irregular case, then validating all workloads again."}}
