{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"The aligned-row change is validated and improved all three irregular workloads by 14–19% with no correctness cost. I’m now testing block ordering: the current 3-D grid interleaves different heads, which weakens cache reuse; a flattened, grouped order can schedule neighboring tiles from the same head and reuse query/key tiles through L2 without persistent workgroups."}}
